Okay - this is both my first post to this group, and my first ascension. 
I've been playing about 2 and a half months, and have learnt alot about
this game quickly, mostly due to the help of #nethack@OPN.  Nevertheless,
I had a comedy of errors along the way to my first ascension.

The character concerned was a Male Chaotic Elven Wizard.  He started with
the usual wizard kit, and no pet, with spellbooks of Force Bolt and
Healing.

I found an altar on dlvl 2, which was not aligned with my alignment.  I
noted this to come back later and convert it, and then rushed to Sokoban,
using Force Bolt copiously and writing Elbereth lots.  When I got to
Sokoban, I id'd the first wand I saw on the first level, and it turned out
to be a wand of wishing !  Thanking the god of RNG, I proceeded to wish
for 2 blessed charging scrolls, blessed +4 silver dragon scale mail,
a magic marker, blessed fixed +4 gauntlets of dexterity (which came out as
cursed -4 gauntlets of dexterity), blessed fixed +4 speed boots and the
master key of thievery (which came out cursed).  I then ate the next
nymph corpse, which gave me teleportitis to go with the teleport control.

Instead of completing sokoban, I journeyed back to the altar on dlvl2,
and converted it.  Then, I went back to the mines, and proceeded to
minetown. My journey to minetown was quite uneventful, however, once I got
there, I stumbled across my own bones file, which had killed my last two
characters.  There were several Mariliths and leocrottas dotted about the
level.  Thankfully, I managed to dispatch these , though not without
hiding for an age inside the temple, and locking doors to two rooms below
which had been dug through into the temple, due to my much improved AC at
the time (something like -13 on an xplvl7 character, the details elude me
:P).  I grabbed everything appropriate from my previous bones files
:(several spellbooks and some assorted less important things).

I then proceeded to head back down to sokoban, and completed sokoban
(though several slips of fingers ended up with me having to do alot of
squeezing on the higher levels.).  By this time, I had I'd enchant weapon,
and had enchanted my Quarterstaff to +5.  Unfortunately, I got a bit
overzealous with Enchant Weapon, and watched as my carefully worked
Quarterstaff exploded in my face.  I grabbed a nearby dropped dagger and
got on with the job at hand.  I cleared the treasure zoo, hoping to find a
bag of holding, but got an amulet of reflection. Obviously, this was not
particularly useful, as I already had SDSM.  I headed out of Sokoban, and
went back to dlvl 2 to store unneeded loot.  I had some potions of water
by then, so I decided to make some holy water. I didn't however, realise
that my god was angry with me, and I was told that he was displeased.
Every time I sacrificed a creature from dlvl 2, I felt that this was
inadequate, so I headed off further into the dungeon to see whether I
could do anything better.

After killing lots more monsters on the way down to dlvl12, I noted
another non-aligned altar there.  As I didn't wish to risk being converted
to that alignment, I ran back to dlvl2, and tried to make holy water
again.  The amount of bloodthirsty killing I had been doing must have
appealed to my god, as my water was duly blessed.  I gathered my
belongings (which were now quite sizable, and included many unidentified
rings and wands), and travelled down to dlvl12, set up a little cache with
a chest, and put all of my temporarily unneeded stuff in there and burnt
Elbereth on the square with a wand of fire.

I then went about repeatedly killing things to increase my favour with my
god.  Soon afterward, my god rewarded me with Magicbane.  I swapped
Magicbane for my dagger, and continued to use that as my main weapon. 
Unfortunately, I was clumsy in two ways after this too.  I had
identified Enchant Armor, and had used my magic marker to write several
enchant armor scrolls, first bringing my gauntlets of dexterity to +2, and
then bringing my cloak of Magic Resistance to +4.  I then went overboard
with it again, and blew up my cloak of Magic Resistance.  You'd think I
would have learned from the Quarterstaff, huh ?  Thankfully, magicbane
provided some limited forms of protection that I would have been missing
otherwise.

After this, I made another fatal error.  A woodland elf came running into
my little base, and I put him back down quickly with Magicbane.  I then
forgot which race I was, and sacrificed the same Elf.  Juiblex was
summoned, and I quaked in fear, as I had never faced a high ranked demon
before.  I walked into him half expecting to die, but found that Juiblex
is certainly not as difficult an opponent as I would have expected. 
Juiblex died quickly, without causing me too many issues.  Unsure as to
whether my god would have been angered by this action, I decided to head
down to kill medusa.  I got to medusa, and force bolted everything I could
see in the surrounding water.  I went in, and battled my way to medusa's
room, where she killed herself by looking at my shiny silver armour.

I then went further down, looking for the castle to gain another wand of
wishing.  I had not, however, yet been given the tune to open the
drawbridge, so I forcebolted the drawbridge down, and used a scroll of
earth to block in the moat.

There were three liches inside the front room of the castle, who started
summoning as soon as all this started.  Thankfully, the gremlins were
peaceful (they had multiplied on a large scale) - I battled my way through
trolls and giants and sharks, into the front room, where all three liches
dropped to magicbane with comparative ease.  I then battled my way through
the castle to the top two keeps, finding a wand of wishing in the second
keep I looked in, and locking myself in the keep.  I wished for more
scrolls of charging, another magic marker, a replacement +4 cloak of magic
resistance, 2 blessed scrolls of genocide (which I hadn't id'd yet), and
spellbooks of magic missile and finger of death, and then read those
spellbooks. Ten seconds after I'd made my final wish, I started to wonder
why I had not wished for a bag of holding.  I blessed genocided ";" and
"R" - I hate instadeath, and there were a large amount of disenchanters
still in the castle that I had avoided on the way in.  I battled my way
back out of the castle and headed back up to level 12, where I stashed
alot of my things, and headed back for the mines.  I headed for the bottom
of the mines, anjoying my new found magic missile.  I got to the bottom,
and drunk a potion of object detection, dug away to get the luckstone down
there and ran back up and then to dlvl12, and blessed it.

I then found the quest portal on level 12, but could not find the secret
door to enter the tower.  Instead, I decided to go down further beyond the
castle.  so I dived down past the castle, finding a magic whistle
and then taming a dog along the way, and bringing him along for the ride.
I cleared the valley of the dead without too many issues - not too shabby,
as this had been my first time below the castle.  I then headed down into
gehennom aimlessly, just exploring.  I lost my dog somehow, and I think he
died.  Soon afterward, I found a black dragon figurine and blessed and
invoked it, and got a black dragon pet.  I'd failed to realise before just
how completely and utterly useless dragons are as pets.  They tend to
avoid fighting, they don't use their breath weapons, and you spend all of
your time waiting for them to finish eating.  Eventually, I got bored of
waiting for him and left him behind.  I then dived further into Gehennom,
for not aparent reason.  I got down to level 42, then decided as I was
getting burdened, that I really should go back and tidy up my inventory
and do the quest.  I got back up to the castle however, and realised one
important mistake.  I'd brought with me no means of getting back across
the castle - no levitation or water walking.  I went back down and decided
to try Vlads tower.  I cleared that easily, finding both the Candelbrum,
and a pair of water walking boots.  (I'd acquired a spellbook of identify
way before this, I forget where).  

I ran back up to level 12, and tidied up my inventory, before trying to
find the secret door to the wizards tower again.  I found it, and started
on the quest.  Due to the fact that I'd learnt magic mapping by that
point, the quest was very easy.  I ran my way up through the tower,
fighting my way through numerous monsters, and finally came face to face
with "The Dark One".

"The Dark One" proved to be annoying, as finger of death did not work
against him and magic missile appeared ineffective, and he kept running
away.  Eventually, I managed to place myself on the stairs back up, and
repeatedly hit him with magicbane until he died.  I took the eye and ran
back to the Green and continued to hold the eye in my main inventory along
with the master key of thievery.

With the Eye, I could now start spellcasting seriously.  I went back down
into Gehennom, and found spellbooks of magic mapping, polymorph and detect
treasure.  After this, I ran down the bottom of gehennom - on the way
there, I found the ring of levitation I had been looking for, and dug out
easy routes for me to get back out on the way back up. It didn't take me
too long to find the vibrating square, which I picked up a bunch of gold
for, and scattered it around the spot. I then went back up searching for
the entrance to rodneys tower. After going too far back up, and coming
back down, I found the entrance and dug in.  I battled my way up through
rodneys tower, not having too many problems.  I reached the top of the
tower, and couldn't be bothered to remove my speed boots, so I used a wand
of cold to freeze the moat, and went to dig in. after I dug in, I
immediately threw a finger of death in, and rodney died.
 however, I didn't realise there was a hellhound waiting around the
corner, and he came out and melted the ice from underneath me.  I took a
nice dip in the moat :P.  After this, I went in and retrieved the book of
the dead, and ran like hell back to level 47.

I went to the square, and performed the invocation process ("Make some
light to read by" , "Ring the bell to get the attention of the audience" ,
"Read the book to them").  I went down the resulting stairs, and blasted
my way through the hordes of undead with magic missile and magicbane.  I
got to the final room, and I started to get in a bit of trouble, so I
backed up into the corridor, and waited for people to sit in a line of 4,
before throwing finger of death or magic missile at them (depending on
whether there were any undead in the row of 4).  I then went further in
and down, and found the temple, where I rang the bell of opening to find
the secret door, and immediately hit the high priest with a finger of
death.  Moloch was angry at me, and blinded me with lightning, but I went
in and took the amulet of Yendor, used a unicorn horn to get rid of the
blindness, and got the hell out.  

On the way back up, I was constantly harassed by Liches of various types.
I concentrated on just getting out, rather than killing everything.  On
the way back up, I found *two* amulets of life saving.  Later on, this
would prove to be important.

I eventually got back to level 12, and prepared for my run to and through
the planes.  Unfortunately, I still hadn't got a bag of holding by this
point, so I had to travel light.  I took one of my blessed magic markers
(the first one had run out, and been charged once too by now anyway) and
10 unwritten scrolls.  I quaffed all of my potions of healing to get my
maximum HP to 107, and sped up to dlvl1, and into the plane of earth.  At
the plane of earth, Rodney himself decided to finally harass me.  I gave
him the finger of death, and he complied.  I then went digging for the
portal.  Whilst trying to cast dig (which rodney had kindly left for me),
I accidentally hit "g" for polymorph, but my memory of the spell was
twisted and I got confused.  At this point, I realised that I would be
able to use this to my advantage.  I went back to the original room, where
Rodney was waiting for me again !  He quickly ate the finger of death
again, and left another spellbook of dig.  I wrote a gold detection
scroll, confused myself and read it, which revealed the location of the
portal to me.  I then dug my way through to the portal, killing several
earth elementals on the way.

Next, the portal took me to the plane of Air, which gave me more problems.
 I wore my ring of levitation to gain control of my movements, and wrote
 another scroll of gold detection and confused myself again.  I found the
 portal, and headed for it, but I hadn't counted on how much nastier the
 Planes Air Elementals were.  The first two I encountered took fingers of
 death whilst inside them to kill, and the second two used up two charges
 from one of the two wands of death I had acquired on my travels (I was
 running low on mana by this point.).  I was down to about half HP (50-60
 ish) by this point, and was starting to worry.

Next, I came to the plane of fire.  I swapped my rings out for a ring of
fire resistance and levitation, and then a large crowd of creatures
attacked me.  I changed the ring of levitation for a ring of conflict, and
watched them battle it out whilst writing another gold detection scroll. 
I removed the ring of conflict, and replaced it with slow digestion, for
some reason I don't recall (most likely stupidity :P).  Immediately, a
vortex attacked me, but since I was fire resistant at this point, I
decided to use the vortex as a shelter.  This turned out to be a very bad
move, and cost me an amulet of life saving.  When I decided to kill the
vortex, I didn't realise that I was over the lava at the time.  I promptly
dropped into the lava with a ton of monsters around me, burning my scroll
of gold detection (the blank scrolls were in my oilskin sack, thankfully).
 I put on my ring of levitation too late, however, and ended up drowning
 in the lava.  That accounted for my first amulet.  I then immediately got
 back out, put on another Amulet of Life saving, wrote another scroll and
 confused myself and found the portal, and dashed for it.  I managed to
 dodge my way through the crowds, and get there.

I got to the water plane, with my ring of levitation on, and wrote the
scroll immediately and just legged it.  I managed to not end up having to
fight anything across the Water plane.

Finally, I got to the Astral plane, where three archliches awaited my
arrival eagerly.  I finally accepted that it was going to be difficult for
me to ascend without killing liches completely.  I wrote a blessed scroll
of genocide, and genocided L completely.  I then replaced the ring of
levitation for the ring of conflict, and watched all the summonees
attacking each other, while I headed for the right hand door.  Pestilence
was behind the right hand door waiting for me.  He made me ill several
times, and summoned large amounts of insects around me.  After curing
myself with the unicorn horn several times, I got fed up with him and
stuck my finger of death up at him.  In my haste to get through, however,
I didn't notice he'd made me Ill one last time.  I died, again.  The
second amulet of life saving saved me, again.  After this, it was a
straight dash.  A couple of angels caused me some minor problems, because
my melee still wasn't that strong.  I didn't realise that Angels held
reflective stuff for the most part, but was most amused when magic missile
bounced between one and myself several times.  I headed for the right hand
altar first, crossing my fingers and hoping for Luck.  The god of RNG was
kind to me again, and I ran to the Altar, to offer up the Amulet to my god.

At 1:20 AM (british time) on the 26th October 2003, I ascended my first
character.  In the IRC channel #nethack on the OPN network - the following
was announced.

01:20 < Rodney> madness (Wiz Elf Mal Cha), 3174302 points, ascended
01:20 < Rodney> madness reaches #127 on the top 2000 list.

I used 10 wishes and genocided (I believe) 12 species.  I never
polymorphed anything, and was never changed myself (though I did displace
a pet onto a polymorph trap at one point).  I never found that bag of
holding, but found with careful stashing, it was not required (but was a
bit of a pain).  I found the eye and the master key of thievery to be a
very good mix, and probably saved me in the planes (bear in mind my max HP
was 111, and my AC was -20).  Interestingly, I *never* used a thrown or
fired projectile weapon.

I hope my comedy of errors amused some of you, and I'm still shocked I
managed to ascend this character, given the mistakes I made along the way.
Sorry that some of the details are sketchy, I didn't take too many notes
along the way.  Credit to all the help I have received learning this game
from the folks at #nethack on OPN.  Now I might be able to get some work
done again ! (But no ! I have to ascend a Monk first !)

Mark

